        '\n' +
        'Learning and training (story commands):\n' +
        '- Only when he trains, studies or takes a lesson NOW is it activity train or study with learn: a KNOWN SKILLS id he practises, a LEARNING id he goes on with, or the kind of a new technique he is taught (strike, bolt, guard, ward, mend). teacher: the PRESENT person who teaches him in this message, else null. tags and aspects: only those his words or the lesson name, else null. minutes or until as he says them.\n' +
        `- Asking to be taught, a wish ("I'd like to learn …", "teach me someday"), a question about a technique, a price or a plan for later is no command: words, the story lets the other answer.\n` +
        '- Studying a manual or primer he holds (OBJECTS: manual · … teaches …) for a time is activity study with material: its id, and learn: the technique it teaches or the LEARNING id he goes on with. Only looking at it or reading its title is no study.\n' +
        '- Activating a Skill Stone he holds (OBJECTS: Skill Stone · … holds …) now is use with its id; wanting to, asking about it or examining it is no command.\n' +
        '- Training a lasting quality of himself NOW, not a technique (conditioning his body, sharpening his mind or senses, hardening his will, building strength or agility), is activity train or study with learn: the core stat it builds (STR strength, VIT toughness, AGI agility, INT mind, PER senses, WIL will), or the LEARNING id he goes on with.\n' +
        '- CLASS CHOICE lists alternative evolved Classes offered by the engine. "I choose <offered name> as my class" is development.accept with that OPTION id (e.g. class.e.offense), never the group id dec.class.e or an invented dec.class.e.offense. Never choose for him. development.decline on its group or option postpones the same choice; it does not discard or reroll it. Questions and wishes book nothing.\n' +
        '- A POSSIBLE PASSIVE or a POSSIBLE SKILL in the CATALOG is a development offered to him, not his yet: development.accept when he clearly takes it now (replace: for a Passive, the PASSIVES id he gives up for it, only when all his slots are held and he names one; else null), development.decline when he clearly lets it pass (passive.accept and passive.decline are older names of the same for a Passive). Thinking it over, asking about it or wanting it later is no command.\n' +
        'Examples (another town): CATALOG: PRESENT: npc.tutor (Brannoc, sword tutor) · KNOWN SKILLS warrior.cleave (Cleave: attack · single target) · LEARNING learn.1 (guard (Defense) from Brannoc, 40/100 LP)\n' +
        '- "*i spend the next two hours with Brannoc drilling the stance he shows me*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"train","what":"the stance Brannoc shows him","minutes":120,"until":null,"learn":"learn.1","teacher":"npc.tutor","tags":null,"aspects":null,"quote":"i spend the next two hours with Brannoc drilling the stance he shows me"}]}\n' +
        '- "*i practise my cleave on the post for an hour*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"train","what":"Cleave on the post","minutes":60,"until":null,"learn":"warrior.cleave","teacher":null,"tags":null,"aspects":null,"quote":"i practise my cleave on the post for an hour"}]}\n' +
        '- "Could you teach me a fire spell some day?" → {"commands":[]}\n' +
        '- (OBJECTS: obj.t4.primer (Primer of the Steady Guard, held by Alaric, manual · F · teaches guard (Defense))) "*i sit down with the primer and work through it for two hours*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"study","what":"the Primer of the Steady Guard","minutes":120,"until":null,"learn":"guard","teacher":null,"tags":null,"aspects":null,"material":"obj.t4.primer","quote":"i sit down with the primer and work through it for two hours"}]}\n' +
