        `…The trouble's been at the ford crossing, evening and dusk, which is exactly when a loaded cart comes late to Reedford. River road's open ground the whole way — no cover for a man on foot to hide in, which cuts both ways. Carts have been robbed, not killed, so far. They take the dye, the drivers keep their teeth." He straightened the ledger and looked at Alaric properly for the first time. "You're Novice, traveling alone. Odell pays for a guard, not a hero — she'll want to see a plate and a staff and nothing more. First light, remember. She won't wait past it, she loses the day's trade."\n` +
