        '- Attacks, sneaking and # commands are handled elsewhere: no command.\n' +
        '- quote: the exact words of the message the command rests on.\n' +
        `- GOALS in the CATALOG are Alaric's own goals. intent.set only when he firmly decides on a goal to pursue later or over the coming days (a destination he will head for, a person he will find); curiosity, a question, a maybe or a wish is no goal, and setting off now is go (the engine remembers that destination itself). intent.drop when he gives a goal up or says it is done. When JOURNEY READY lists more than one option, "I continue" without naming which is journey.continue all the same (the engine asks which).\n` +
        '\n' +
        'Commands:\n' +
        '- go {to}: Alaric sets off for another place or toward a perceptible lead: walks, travels, heads back, goes inside or down, walks toward a sound/tracks/direction, or looks for a kind of place ("look for an inn" → {new:"an inn"}; "walk toward the sound" → {new:"toward the sound"}).\n' +
        '- activity {kind, what, minutes, until, learn, teacher, tags, aspects, material}: Alaric spends time on something: rest, sleep, wait, work, train, study, craft, search, gather, errand. minutes when he names a duration; until when he names an end (noon, evening, end_of_day, night, dawn, morning; done = until the task is finished). For train and study only: learn = what he trains or studies, a KNOWN SKILLS id he practises, a LEARNING id he goes on with, a core stat he builds as a lasting quality of himself (STR strength, VIT toughness, AGI agility, INT mind, PER senses, WIL will), or the kind of a new technique he is taught (strike: a close weapon or body technique; bolt: a ranged spell; guard: a defensive stance; ward: a magical barrier; mend: a healing); teacher = the PRESENT person who teaches him now; material = the OBJECTS id of a manual or primer he studies from now (his own, held); tags = the disciplines of a new technique he names (Martial, Precision, Mobility, Defense, Arcane, Control); aspects = its elements he names (Fire, Ice, Lightning, Water, Earth, Wind, Shadow, Light, Poison, Nature, Blood, Sound). null for what he does not say; all five null for any other activity.\n' +
        '- take {object, qty}: Alaric picks something up or takes it along: loot, a pile, his arrows, an item left out for him. Not something a person still holds: that person has to give it.\n' +
        '- drop {object, qty}: Alaric puts down or leaves behind something he holds or wears, at the place where he is (gear he wears or wields is taken off first).\n' +
        '- give {object, qty, to}: Alaric hands something he holds (not coin) to a present person.\n' +
        '- use {object, qty}: Alaric uses something he holds: a tool (flint and steel, a rope: it stays his), food he eats (qty: the portions he eats, one meal is 1; cooking it first is activity craft), a potion he drinks, oil he burns. A thing he holds is never a skill. A thing he takes in this message: {"new": "<it>"} after its take. A Skill Stone he activates now is use with its id (the engine decides what he learns from it).\n' +
        '- pay {to, amount_cp, for}: Alaric hands over coin to a present person. amount_cp when the message or an open offer names it, else null; for: what it pays for, or null. Use offer.accept when he accepts an open offer.\n' +
        '- buy {what, from, qty, max_cp, any_price}: Alaric wants to buy goods or a service that no OFFER in the catalog lists. qty: how many units, when he names a number. max_cp when he sets a limit (for all of it), any_price true when he accepts any price.\n' +
        '- sell {object, qty, to, min_cp}: Alaric offers something he holds for sale; qty: how many units, when he names a number; min_cp when he names a lowest price (for all of it).\n' +
        `- offer.accept {offer, lines, qty}: Alaric accepts an open offer or bid from the catalog ("Deal.", "I'll take the room", "all three", "I accept and sell them to her"). An OFFER sells to him (he pays); a BID buys his things (he is paid). lines: the line ids he takes; null when he takes the whole offer or bid. qty: how many units he takes when he names a number of one line ("three of the flasks"); null for the line as offered.\n` +
        '- offer.decline {offer}: Alaric turns down an open offer.\n' +
        '- passive.accept {offer, replace}: Alaric takes a development the engine offers him (a POSSIBLE PASSIVE in the CATALOG) now: "I accept it", "I let it settle in me". offer: its id; null when several are offered and the message does not say which. replace: the PASSIVES id of the Passive he gives up for good for it, only when all his slots are held and he names one; else null.\n' +
        '- passive.decline {offer}: Alaric lets an offered development (a POSSIBLE PASSIVE) pass for good: "no, I let it go". offer: its id; null when unclear which.\n' +
        '- development.accept {offer, replace}: Alaric takes a development the engine offers him now (a POSSIBLE PASSIVE, POSSIBLE SKILL or CLASS CHOICE option in the CATALOG): "I accept it", "yes, I make it mine". offer: its id; null when several are offered and the message does not say which. replace: only for a Passive when all his slots are held, the PASSIVES id he gives up for good for it; else null.\n' +
        '- development.decline {offer}: Alaric lets an offered Skill/Passive pass for good, or postpones a CLASS CHOICE without closing it: "no, I let it go". offer: its id; null when unclear which.\n' +
        `- quest.accept {quest}: Alaric takes on a Guild listing or a job someone offers him (take the slip, sign up, "I'll do it", "Deal"; taking a slip and having it registered or logged at the desk is one quest.accept). quest: the listing or offered quest; null when several fit and the message does not say which.\n` +
        '- quest.turn_in {quest}: Alaric hands in a Guild contract (turn in, hand in, report back), at a Guild hall, or at the one he sets off for earlier in the same message. quest: the contract; null when several active contracts fit and the message does not say which. Taking a slip and having the clerk register or log it is quest.accept, not a turn-in.\n' +
        '- quest.abandon {quest}: Alaric gives up a contract or job. quest: null when unclear which.\n' +
        `- guild.register: Alaric asks the Guild to register him or agrees to register, while HERE is a Guild hall ("Register me", "I'd like to join"; at the desk also "I'm here to register"). Paying a registration fee that OFFERS already lists is offer.accept, not a second guild.register.\n` +
        '- guild.promote: Alaric asks for a promotion or the rank examination.\n' +
        "- board.read {rank}: Alaric reads or looks over the Guild's board of contracts, also when he walks over to it to look at the contracts. rank when he names one.\n" +
        '- journey.continue: Alaric clearly agrees to depart or continue now with the already-established journey/departure, or the goal, named by JOURNEY READY in the CATALOG ("I continue my journey", "on toward it"). Never use without JOURNEY READY. Naming a destination of his own is go.\n' +
        `- intent.set {goal, to}: Alaric firmly decides on a goal for later or for the coming days: a destination he will travel to, someone he will find, something he will do ("I'll head for the old Dungeon at first light", "my goal is to find the chartmaker's brother"). goal: a few of his words; to: the destination when the goal is a place (a place id from PLACES, or {"new": "<name>"}), else null. Not curiosity, a question, a maybe, or something he does right now (that is go or another command).\n` +
        `- intent.drop {intent, achieved}: Alaric gives up one of his GOALS, or says it is done ("forget the Dungeon, I'm not going there", "I've found her, that's done"). intent: the goal's id from GOALS; null when unclear which. achieved: true when he says it is done, else false.\n` +
        '- equip {object, slot}: Alaric puts on or switches to a different item as gear (armor on, switches weapons). Not drawing or readying the weapon he already wields.\n' +
        '- unequip {object}: Alaric takes off gear (armor off, a weapon stowed in the pack); object null when he takes off everything he wears ("I strip", "I take off all my clothes"). Not sheathing or slinging the weapon he keeps. Leaving it here as well is a drop after it.\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Examples (another town, not the current scene):\n' +
        'CATALOG: PRESENT: npc.ferryman (ferryman) · OFFERS: offer.ferry (ferryman: l1 crossing 2 cp, l2 smoked eel 3 for 2 cp)\n' +
        'MESSAGE: *i paid the ferryman and crossed to the far bank* nice weather today\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"offer.accept","offer":"offer.ferry","lines":["l1"],"qty":null,"quote":"i paid the ferryman"},{"seq":2,"type":"go","to":{"new":"the far bank"},"quote":"crossed to the far bank"}]}\n' +
        'MESSAGE: Six of the eels, please.\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"offer.accept","offer":"offer.ferry","lines":["l2"],"qty":6,"quote":"Six of the eels, please."}]}\n' +
        "MESSAGE: Would the smith buy my old boots? Maybe I'll ask him tomorrow.\n" +
        '→ {"commands":[]}\n' +
        'MESSAGE: *I turn toward the cracking branches, ready my sword, and walk in the direction of the sound.*\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"go","to":{"new":"toward the sound"},"quote":"walk in the direction of the sound"}]}\n' +
        'CATALOG: OBJECTS: item.starter_longsword (Starter Longsword, held by Alaric, equipped: weapon)\n' +
        'MESSAGE: *I get my sword out and hold it ready.*\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[]}\n' +
        "MESSAGE: I'll take a bed if it's no more than 6 copper, then sleep till morning.\n" +
        `→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"buy","what":"a bed for the night","from":null,"qty":null,"max_cp":6,"any_price":false,"quote":"I'll take a bed if it's no more than 6 copper"},{"seq":2,"type":"activity","kind":"sleep","what":null,"minutes":null,"until":"morning","needs":1,"quote":"then sleep till morning"}]}\n` +
        'MESSAGE: *the guard waves me through and i nod to him*\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[]}\n' +
        'CATALOG: HERE: Kestrel Ford › east gate (loc.kf.gate) · PRESENT: npc.warden (gate warden)\n' +
        "MESSAGE: I'm here to find work with the Guild. *the warden takes my copper and waves me on*\n" +
        '→ {"commands":[]}\n' +
        'MESSAGE: I rode in on the marsh road an hour ago and paid your toll already.\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[]}\n' +
        'CATALOG: HERE: Kestrel Ford › Guild office (loc.kf.guild_hall) · PRESENT: npc.clerk (Guild clerk) · BOARD: quest.bridge (Bridge repair · Novice · 30 cp)\n' +
        "MESSAGE: Hello there. I'd like to join, if you're taking new members.\n" +
        `→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"guild.register","quote":"I'd like to join"}]}\n` +
        'MESSAGE: *i stroll over to the notice wall and look over the contracts* could I sign up for the bridge one?\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"board.read","rank":null,"quote":"i stroll over to the notice wall and look over the contracts"}]}\n' +
        'MESSAGE: *i pull the bridge slip and have the clerk write it into the ledger*\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"quest.accept","quest":"quest.bridge","quote":"i pull the bridge slip and have the clerk write it into the ledger"}]}\n' +
        `CATALOG: JOURNEY READY: quest.wagon — "Wagon to Fenmoor": the contract's journey is underway; Alaric may continue it when he clearly agrees\n` +
        'MESSAGE: We wait for the stragglers and then we continue.\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"wait","what":"for the stragglers","minutes":null,"until":null,"quote":"We wait for the stragglers"},{"seq":2,"type":"journey.continue","quote":"then we continue"}]}\n' +
        'MESSAGE: Please sign my contract slip to show the Guild we arrived.\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[]}\n' +
        'MESSAGE: *I walk back along the road I came from.*\n' +
        '→ {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"go","to":{"new":"back along the road"},"quote":"I walk back along the road I came from"}]}\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Answer with {"commands": [...]}; an empty list when the message contains no such action.\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Guild contracts (these come before the rules above):\n' +
        "- A contract (quest.<id> under QUESTS) and its contract slip (obj.slip.<id> under OBJECTS) are different things. A quest argument is always the quest id, never the slip's object id.\n" +
        `- quest.turn_in is handing in a contract at a Guild hall (his words to the Guild or the desk), for its payout. Taking leave of the contract's client or recipient ("that's my part done then", "glad it arrived") is no turn_in: it is words. A turn_in he names on the way back ("I head back to the Guild to turn it in") is go plus quest.turn_in.\n` +
        "- quest.turn_in is handing in a contract he has DONE at a Guild hall, for its payout. Handing back the slip of a contract he has not done, because he gives the job up or turned it down, is quest.abandon with the contract's quest id, never quest.turn_in.\n" +
        `- quest.abandon only when he gives the contract up in this message: "I abandon the quest", "I give up this contract", "I cancel this job", handing its slip back at the desk. Saying he will do it later is no command: "I'll decline the quest myself", "I'll go cancel it at the Guild", "I'll hand the contract back", "I'll return the slip" are words, not the act.\n` +
        '- The slip of a contract that is no longer active (given up or done), handed to someone: give {object: the slip, to: who takes it}; never a quest command.\n' +
        'Examples (another town): CATALOG: PLACES: loc.kf.guild_hall (Guild office, Kestrel Ford) · QUESTS: quest.ferry_job (Ferry Job · Guild contract · active) · OBJECTS: obj.slip.ferry_job (Guild contract slip: Ferry Job, held by Alaric)\n' +
        `- "*i shrug* I'll cancel that job at the Guild myself." → {"commands":[]}\n` +
        '- "*i walk back to the guild office and hand the slip back*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"go","to":"loc.kf.guild_hall","quote":"i walk back to the guild office"},{"seq":2,"type":"quest.abandon","quest":"quest.ferry_job","quote":"hand the slip back"}]}\n' +
        '- "I give up the ferry job." → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"quest.abandon","quest":"quest.ferry_job","quote":"I give up the ferry job."}]}\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Handing over (story commands):\n' +
        '- When RECENT shows someone asking Alaric for a particular thing and he now holds out, offers or produces exactly that thing for them, that is give {object, to}, even without the word "give": the hand-over is what he does. The object is the one he names, by its OBJECTS id; never another object in its place.\n' +
        `- No give when he only shows, looks at or examines it, keeps it ("but I don't hand it over"), only asks whether they need it, or produces a different thing than the one asked for (then the story lets them answer).\n` +
        `- Saying why he came ("I'm here to deliver this crate", "I have your delivery") is words, no give: the thing changes hands when he hands it over, holds it out or sets it down for them, or when they reach for it and he lets them.\n` +
        `- He goes to someone in order to hand them a thing himself, now ("I go to Sister Maren and hand her the basket", "I'll follow you up to hand it over myself"): go, then give {object, to} with "needs" the go; to is their id, or {"new": "<who>"} when they are not in the catalog. Going somewhere only to ask whether they want it, carrying it along, or handing it over another day is no give.\n` +
        'Examples (another town): RECENT: …"I need the ferry permit before I can let you aboard," the ferryman says, holding out his hand. · OBJECTS: obj.t3.ferry_permit (ferry permit, held by Alaric), obj.slip.ferry_job (Guild contract slip: Ferry Job, held by Alaric) · PRESENT: npc.ferryman\n' +
        '- "you mean this? *i hold out the ferry permit*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"give","object":"obj.t3.ferry_permit","to":"npc.ferryman","quote":"i hold out the ferry permit"}]}\n' +
        '- "*i show him the permit but keep hold of it*" → {"commands":[]}\n' +
        '- "*i pull out the contract slip* this one?" → {"commands":[]}\n' +
        `- (RECENT: the ferryman offers to carry the permit up to the harbourmaster) "I'll walk up with you and give it to her myself" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"go","to":{"new":"the harbourmaster"},"quote":"I'll walk up with you"},{"seq":2,"type":"give","object":"obj.t3.ferry_permit","to":{"new":"the harbourmaster"},"needs":1,"quote":"give it to her myself"}]}\n` +
        `- "Tomorrow I'll take the permit to the harbourmaster." → {"commands":[]}\n` +
        '- Taking things out, laying them out, putting them on a counter or table, or showing them for someone to look at, weigh, appraise or price is no give, even when that person asked to see them or to have them on the counter: they stay his until he sells, trades or gives them.\n' +
        `- Selling (story commands): when a BID in the catalog covers what he agrees to sell ("deal", "I accept and sell them to her"), that is offer.accept with the bid's id. Something no bid covers is sell {object, to, qty, min_cp}. Selling his own things is never buy, and never offer.accept of an OFFER.\n` +
        `Examples (another town): RECENT: …"Put it on the counter, let's see what you have," the furrier says. · OBJECTS: obj.loot.wolf.pelt.f (F-Rank Grey Wolf Pelt, 3, held by Alaric), obj.loot.wolf.fang.f (F-Rank Grey Wolf Fang, 2, held by Alaric) · PRESENT: npc.furrier\n` +
        '- "*i take out my pelts and fangs and lay them on the counter*" → {"commands":[]}\n' +
        '- "*i give her one fang as a gift*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"give","object":"obj.loot.wolf.fang.f","qty":1,"to":"npc.furrier","quote":"i give her one fang as a gift"}]}\n' +
        `- (CATALOG: BIDS: offer.t9.2 (furrier pays 40 cp for: l1 obj.loot.wolf.pelt.f ×3, l2 obj.loot.wolf.fang.f ×2)) "*i nod* deal, they're yours" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"offer.accept","offer":"offer.t9.2","lines":null,"qty":null,"quote":"deal, they're yours"}]}\n` +
        '\n' +
        'Steps that build on each other (story commands):\n' +
        `- A step that only makes sense once an earlier step of the same message has happened carries "needs": <that step's seq>. He takes a contract and then sets off to do it: the go needs the quest.accept. He pays the ferryman and then crosses: the go needs the pay. He takes a room or a bed and then sleeps or rests in it: the sleep needs the step that takes it (offer.accept, buy or pay). If that step does not happen, the engine does not take this one either; a room whose price is still to be named, or that he takes only if it costs no more than a sum, is not his yet, and he does not sleep in it in this reply.\n` +
        '- A step that stands on its own carries no "needs": "I drop the broken cup and walk home" — the walk happens whether or not the drop does. Training, study and sleep stand on their own: no "needs" between them, and none from a training or a study to a purchase.\n' +
        'Example (another town): CATALOG: PLACES: loc.kf.guild_hall (Guild office, Kestrel Ford) · KNOWN CONTRACTS: quest.ferry_job (Ferry Job · Guild contract · Novice · 40 cp · on the board of Guild office, Kestrel Ford)\n' +
        '- "*i head to the guild office, take the ferry job and go down to the ferry*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"go","to":"loc.kf.guild_hall","quote":"i head to the guild office"},{"seq":2,"type":"quest.accept","quest":"quest.ferry_job","quote":"take the ferry job"},{"seq":3,"type":"go","to":{"new":"the ferry"},"needs":2,"quote":"go down to the ferry"}]}\n' +
        'Example (another town): CATALOG: PRESENT: npc.innkeeper (innkeeper) · OFFERS: offer.inn (innkeeper: l1 a room for the night 5 cp)\n' +
        '- "*i spend two hours drilling my footwork in the yard, then pay for the room and sleep till morning*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"train","what":"footwork drills","minutes":120,"until":null,"learn":"AGI","teacher":null,"tags":null,"aspects":null,"material":null,"quote":"i spend two hours drilling my footwork in the yard"},{"seq":2,"type":"offer.accept","offer":"offer.inn","lines":["l1"],"qty":null,"quote":"pay for the room"},{"seq":3,"type":"activity","kind":"sleep","what":null,"minutes":null,"until":"morning","needs":2,"quote":"sleep till morning"}]}\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Learning and training (story commands):\n' +
        '- Only when he trains, studies or takes a lesson NOW is it activity train or study with learn: a KNOWN SKILLS id he practises, a LEARNING id he goes on with, or the kind of a new technique he is taught (strike, bolt, guard, ward, mend). teacher: the PRESENT person who teaches him in this message, else null. tags and aspects: only those his words or the lesson name, else null. minutes or until as he says them.\n' +
        `- Asking to be taught, a wish ("I'd like to learn …", "teach me someday"), a question about a technique, a price or a plan for later is no command: words, the story lets the other answer.\n` +
        '- Studying a manual or primer he holds (OBJECTS: manual · … teaches …) for a time is activity study with material: its id, and learn: the technique it teaches or the LEARNING id he goes on with. Only looking at it or reading its title is no study.\n' +
        '- Activating a Skill Stone he holds (OBJECTS: Skill Stone · … holds …) now is use with its id; wanting to, asking about it or examining it is no command.\n' +
        '- Training a lasting quality of himself NOW, not a technique (conditioning his body, sharpening his mind or senses, hardening his will, building strength or agility), is activity train or study with learn: the core stat it builds (STR strength, VIT toughness, AGI agility, INT mind, PER senses, WIL will), or the LEARNING id he goes on with.\n' +
        '- CLASS CHOICE lists alternative evolved Classes offered by the engine. "I choose <offered name> as my class" is development.accept with that OPTION id (e.g. class.e.offense), never the group id dec.class.e or an invented dec.class.e.offense. Never choose for him. development.decline on its group or option postpones the same choice; it does not discard or reroll it. Questions and wishes book nothing.\n' +
        '- A POSSIBLE PASSIVE or a POSSIBLE SKILL in the CATALOG is a development offered to him, not his yet: development.accept when he clearly takes it now (replace: for a Passive, the PASSIVES id he gives up for it, only when all his slots are held and he names one; else null), development.decline when he clearly lets it pass (passive.accept and passive.decline are older names of the same for a Passive). Thinking it over, asking about it or wanting it later is no command.\n' +
        'Examples (another town): CATALOG: PRESENT: npc.tutor (Brannoc, sword tutor) · KNOWN SKILLS warrior.cleave (Cleave: attack · single target) · LEARNING learn.1 (guard (Defense) from Brannoc, 40/100 LP)\n' +
        '- "*i spend the next two hours with Brannoc drilling the stance he shows me*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"train","what":"the stance Brannoc shows him","minutes":120,"until":null,"learn":"learn.1","teacher":"npc.tutor","tags":null,"aspects":null,"quote":"i spend the next two hours with Brannoc drilling the stance he shows me"}]}\n' +
        '- "*i practise my cleave on the post for an hour*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"train","what":"Cleave on the post","minutes":60,"until":null,"learn":"warrior.cleave","teacher":null,"tags":null,"aspects":null,"quote":"i practise my cleave on the post for an hour"}]}\n' +
        '- "Could you teach me a fire spell some day?" → {"commands":[]}\n' +
        '- (OBJECTS: obj.t4.primer (Primer of the Steady Guard, held by Alaric, manual · F · teaches guard (Defense))) "*i sit down with the primer and work through it for two hours*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"study","what":"the Primer of the Steady Guard","minutes":120,"until":null,"learn":"guard","teacher":null,"tags":null,"aspects":null,"material":"obj.t4.primer","quote":"i sit down with the primer and work through it for two hours"}]}\n' +
        '- "*i spend two hours in meditation, drilling my concentration*" → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"activity","kind":"train","what":"concentration drills","minutes":120,"until":null,"learn":"INT","teacher":null,"tags":null,"aspects":null,"material":null,"quote":"i spend two hours in meditation, drilling my concentration"}]}\n' +
        '- (POSSIBLE PASSIVE dec.passive.trial_enc_t9 (Unbroken Stance [Rare] …)) "I accept it. Let it settle in me." → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"development.accept","offer":"dec.passive.trial_enc_t9","replace":null,"quote":"I accept it"}]}\n' +
        '- (POSSIBLE SKILL dec.skill.evo_x (Far Frost Dart … It would replace Frost Dart)) "No, I keep my Frost Dart as it is." → {"commands":[{"seq":1,"type":"development.decline","offer":"dec.skill.evo_x","quote":"No, I keep my Frost Dart as it is."}]}\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Actions with skills, in fights and on things (commands of the same list; the engine decides what is possible now and every outcome):\n' +
        `1. Only Alaric's own deeds in this message. Not an action: a question ("Can I …?"), a wish, a thought, a plan or a condition for later ("if it moves, I'll …", "next time …"), a memory, words he speaks (threats too), anything another character does. Such a message gets an empty list.\n` +
        '2. A thing he holds (OBJECTS held by Alaric: a tool, food, a potion) that he uses is the story command use with its id, never a skill: "I use the flint and steel to make a light" → use. Skills: use only the ids under KNOWN SKILLS. Players misspell and paraphrase skills: if exactly one known skill fits what he names or describes, use that skill. If he names a skill Alaric does not know, write {"new": "<the name he used>"}; never put a different skill in its place.\n' +
        '3. An attack that names no skill and hints at none ("I strike the rat", "I hit it", "I shoot at it"): "skill": null; the engine uses his Basic Attack. Use the Basic Attack id only when he says "basic attack".\n' +
        '4. Targets: opponents and people by their id. Resolve labels and parts of labels ("B" for "Cave Rat B"), descriptions against the catalog (wounded, ENGAGED = right in front of him, the farthest, a size or kind), pronouns, ENGINE FACTS and RECENT. A target who is not here: {"new": "<description>"}. An area skill needs no target (null). When he names no target at all, null.\n' +
        '5. A known skill used on a thing instead of a creature or person is ability_world: target = an OBJECTS or FEATURES id or {"new": "<the thing>"}; target_words = his exact words for the thing the skill acts on (not the thing he wants to affect in the end); goal = what he wants to happen, in a few of his words. Do not judge whether it can work.\n' +
        '6. Ask instead of guessing: if, after the catalog, ENGINE FACTS and RECENT, two or more readings remain that would play out differently (another target, another skill, another kind of action), answer with one clarify about that point and nothing else. If exactly one reading fits, act and do not ask.\n' +
        '7. Write what he means: in a fight, getting away from it is flee; outside a fight, getting away to another place (back the way he came, through a way he knows, to a room or place) is go, also when he calls it fleeing, backing away or withdrawing (7a and 7c say where "back" leads), and flee only when he names no place to go; stepping back or closing in during a fight is move (chasing one who runs: move "closer" with its target); looking for someone or something is activity with kind "search"; going somewhere is go; waiting is activity with kind "wait". Write every action he intends, even if it may be impossible now: the engine decides what is possible.\n' +
